:: Mom Has It Tough [event mom_quest] {"position":"3025,1200","size":"100,100"}
The living room is mostly dark. Some sitcom is murmuring away on the TV, a laugh track cheering at jokes nobody is listening to, and $mom.callName is sunk so deep into the couch she might as well be part of it. There's a bottle of cheap red on the coffee table, already half gone, and she's topping up her glass with a hand that isn't quite steady. Her eyes are red at the rims, and the whole room smells like her perfume and wine.

<<Video "images/characters/mom/events/mom has it tough/wine.webm" "" "" 500>>

I stop in the doorway and watch her take a long swallow. I've never seen her like this. She's always been the one who holds everything together, the one who comes home from work and still asks how //my// day was. Seeing her fall apart should make me want to fix it, and it does, but a much quieter part of me has already started doing the math.

<<silently>>
    <<set _msgs = [
        { who: $player, text: "Rough day, $mom.callName? You look like you could use a refill. Or three." },
        { text: "She jumps a little, the glass stopping halfway to her mouth." },
        { who: $mom, text: "Oh, $player.name... yeah. God, I hate that man. I swear, if I have one more day like this one..." },
        { who: $player, text: "Whoa. I thought it was just the workload. What happened?" },
        { text: "She lets out a short, humorless laugh and stares into her glass like the answer might be at the bottom." },
        { who: $mom, text: "Where do I even start? He talks down to everybody, but with the women it's different, it's all these little comments and hints, always with that smile, and ugh, it makes my skin crawl just thinking about it. And because I don't play along, he takes it out on me. Today he yelled at me in front of the whole office, honey, over a report he signed off on himself last week." },
        { who: $player, text: "That's harassment. You know that, right?" },
        { who: $mom, text: "Of course I know, sweetie. But he's the boss, and he plays golf with half the people who could do anything about it, so I'm not going to win that one. I'll just smile and get through it, the way I always do." },
        { who: $player, text: "That's so messed up." },
        { text: "Neither of us says anything for a while. The laugh track goes off again, which doesn't help." },
        { who: $player, text: "Okay, this might sound a little weird, but what if I came by your work sometime with the prototype? Just to take the edge off when he gets like that." },
        { who: $mom, text: "Bring it to the office? Honey, how would that even work?" },
        { who: $player, text: "Same as last time. You remember how much calmer you were afterwards, right?" },
        { who: $mom, text: "Well, it did help, I'll give you that, I slept like a baby. But what would everybody at work think, me sitting there with my $mom.playerRelation and his little gadget like it's bring-your-kid-to-work day?" },
        { who: $player, text: "They'd think you have a $mom.playerRelation who brings you lunch. Come on, it can't hurt to try. Unless you'd rather quit?" },
        { who: $mom, text: "Oh, I wish, sweetie. But this house doesn't pay for itself, and neither does your $sister.relation's tuition." },
        { text: "She swirls the wine around for a moment, then sighs and leans her head back against the couch." },
        { who: $mom, text: "Okay, fine, we'll try it. Once. Now be a dear and fill this up for me before that laugh track drives me crazy." },
    ]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I pour her another glass, a generous one. She thanks me without looking, eyes already drifting back to the TV, and halfway into the next episode she falls asleep with the glass still in her hand. I take it from her before it tips over.

If it's this bad on the days she does everything right, I can't help wondering what he'd do to her if she ever actually made a mistake.

